From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:35:32 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: drive T6040 GPU memory demand from publication
 and continuous idle

T6040 keeps the GFX supplier powered for the firmware's lifetime, as its
PMGR DT documents. Using that supplier as CLPC demand therefore pins DCS 5 /
fabric 2 even after the GPU cores gate. Neo's activity-following supplier is
not a valid T6040 idle witness.

Add a DT-selected CLPC demand consumer. Every actual GPU publication asserts
it, including off-lock direct publication. The existing race-checked 16 ms
continuous-idle effort clear releases it; quarantined work does not count as
execution. CLPC retains its existing 32 ms hold and CPU arbitration. Firmware
shutdown and consumer destruction clear the request. An independent refcounted
request allocation is safe across provider removal, and a device link orders
the supplier. The hot path uses only a leaf spinlock, with no sleeping call,
allocation or GPU callback. Missing requested providers defer probe.

Expose last requested floor, reason bits and host timestamps alongside actual
PMC readback, and expose safe core-power plus last publication time in the
read-only G17 firmware_reports view. Generic runtime PM remains distinct from
firmware core gating: do not relabel unsupported generic PM as active/suspended.
Keep Neo's existing PMGR input and all voltages, floors and delays unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 32f7efefcb39734a758d8dbbd3708099f288c067)
[j604: 99725fd078 ("soc: apple: clpc: expose the graphics input holding the memory floor") is not
 picked: 1.604 already exposes that input through the streaming gate and read-error count, and upstream
 merge d3f1307755 dropped its fields the same way]
[j604: dropped hunk for arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6040.dtsi, absent in 1.604]
[j604: dropped hunk for drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/reports.rs, absent in 1.604]
[j604: conflicts resolved onto 1.604's T8140 streaming gate exactly as upstream merge d3f1307755 did: the PMGR
 input stays apple_clpc_gpu_streaming() with its floor-release count, reason bit 4 is "streaming_gpu" and bit 8
 (read_error) is not used, the host GPU input applies only where the PMGR input is not the demand
 (!hw->gpu_demand) and is maxed with the CPU demand, 1.604's optional apple,gpu-power-state probe and status
 lines are kept, and the Makefile and apple,agx.yaml keep 1.604's object list and reg-names (adds only
 g17/clpc.o and the two new properties)]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
